# SWC-DB Architecture Overview

C++20 Super Wide Column DBMS. Full map: root `AGENTS.md`.

## Modules (`src/cc/{include,lib,bin}/swcdb/`)

- `core` — logging, exceptions, config, `comm/` networking
- `common` — shared header-only helpers
- `db` — cells, columns, protocol, client, SQL
- `fs` — FS interface + Local/Ceph/Hadoop/Broker backends
- `manager` / `ranger` / `broker` / `fsbroker` / `thrift` — daemons
- `utils` — CLI shells

## Daemons

Clients → `swcdbBroker` / `swcdbThriftBroker` → `swcdbManager` (metadata) → `swcdbRanger` (storage) → `swcdbFsBroker` / `libswcdb_fs_*`.

## Namespaces

`SWC::<Module>` mirrors directories. Process state: `SWC::Env::*`. Protocol: `SWC::Comm::Protocol::{Rgr,Mngr,Bkr}`.

When planning features, place code in the matching module; do not invent parallel trees outside `swcdb/`.
